%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
     CALCULATION OF PSEUDOSPIN HAMILTONIAN TENSORS FOR THE MULTIPLET 1 ( effective S =  1/2)
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
The pseudospin is defined in the basis of the following spin-orbit states:
spin-orbit state 1; energy(1) =       0.000 cm-1.
spin-orbit state 2; energy(2) =       0.000 cm-1.
Tunnelling splitting:     0.0000000000 cm-1.

    g TENSOR:
--------------------------------------------------------|
    MAIN VALUES    |             MAIN MAGNETIC AXES     |   x , y , z  -- initial Cartesian axes
-------------------|----|   ----- x ------- y ------- z ---|
Xm, Ym, Zm -- main magnetic axes
 gX =   0.00000000000000 | Xm |  0.01268439357594 -0.99991954984369  0.00000000006251 |
 gY =   0.00000000000000 | Ym |  0.99991954984369  0.01268439357594 -0.00000000011232 |
 gZ =  20.01159652180468 | Zm |  0.00000000011152  0.00000000006393  1.00000000000000 |
--------------------------------------------------------|
CHECK-SIGN parameter =   -5.526600
The sign of the product gX * gY * gZ for multiplet 1: < 0.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECOMPOSITION OF THE MAGNETIC MOMENT Mu_i IN IRREDUCIBLE TENSOR OPERATORS (ITO):
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The quantization axis is the main magnetic axis of this multiplet (Zm).
********************************************************************************
   Mu_i = SUM_{n,m}: [ B(i,n,m) * O(n,m) +  C(i,n,m) * W(n,m) ]
where:
   O(n,m) =  0.5 * ( (-1)**m * Y(n,+m) + Y(n,-m) );
   W(n,m) = -0.5 * ( (-1)**m * Y(n,+m) - Y(n,-m) ) * I;   (I = imaginary unit)
   n - the rank of the ITO, = 1, 3, 5, ... 2*spin;
   m - the component of the ITO, = 0, 1, ... n;
   i - the Cartesian projection of the magnetic moment, i = x,y,z;
These operators have been defined in: 
  L. F. Chibotaru, L.Ungur, J. Chem. Phys., 137, 064112 (2012).
---------------------------------------------------------------|
  n  |  m  | i |        B(i,n,m)       |        C(i,n,m)       |
-----|-----|---|-----------------------|-----------------------|
  1  |  0  | X | -2.06795153330850E-25 |  0.00000000000000E+00 |
  1  |  0  | Y | -4.13590404884127E-25 |  0.00000000000000E+00 |
  1  |  0  | Z | -2.00115965218047E+01 |  0.00000000000000E+00 |
     |-----|---|-----------------------|-----------------------|
  1  |  1  | X | -7.21007475705078E-17 |  5.77033630776590E-17 |
  1  |  1  | Y | -2.66204678319296E-17 | -8.73860341122060E-17 |
  1  |  1  | Z | -2.29842258754722E-15 |  2.86420922614160E-27 |
---------------------------------------------------------------|


********************************************************************************
   Mu_i = SUM_{k,q} * [ B(i,k,q) * O(k,q) ];
where:
   O(k,q) =  Extended Stevens Operators (ESO) as defined in:
          1. Rudowicz, C.; J.Phys.C: Solid State Phys.,18(1985) 1415-1430.
          2. Implemented in the "EasySpin" function in MATLAB, www.easyspin.org.
   k - the rank of the ITO, = 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11;
   q - the component of the ITO, = -k, -k+1, ... 0, 1, ... k;
Knm are proportionality coefficients between the ESO and operators defined in 
J. Chem. Phys., 137, 064112 (2012).
---------------------------------------------------|
